    ## What Masaha is

    > ## Built

    This section lists a capability only once it is merged and working. Each line links the
    capability's document, which
    says what it does.
    - [Occupancy](../features/occupancy.md): on the API, a space's private capacity, set by its
    owner, and its state now
    for its staff: who is present, the count and the live status, with the manual override its staff
    set and clear.
    > - [Finance](../features/finance.md): on the API, a space's income for a month and its windows,
    the staff's
    collections, who owes and who is in credit with the totals, who paid in a month, and the
    occupancy statistics — the
    owner's alone; on the dashboard, the owner's «المالية والتقارير»: a month's income, who owes,
    with the WhatsApp
    reminder, and who paid, each exported as a CSV built in the browser, and the occupancy.
    - [Overview](../features/overview.md): on the API, the owner's overview, a work queue of counts
    with no amount, and
    the admin's, the platform's tiles and the spaces with incomplete data; on the dashboard, «نظرة
    عامة», the owner's
    landing and the admin's.

    > ## Committed scope — v1

    ### Roles
    - Directory of spaces: the list **or** the map, one at a time, the list by default; search and
    filters (area, price,
    student prices, open on Friday, verified, available now); sort, including nearest to me.
    > - Near me: the device's location, rounded on the device and sent in a header only to sort by
    distance, never stored
    or logged (the owner's change, 2026-10-13: it was never sent), with an area or a pin on the map
    as fallbacks ([the
    rule](../frontend/design-system/foundation.md#13-screens-to-design-32), under *Directory*;
    [security ›
    Location](../backend/security.md#location)). Home shows the nearest spaces when a location is in
    use, otherwise the
    spaces available now.
    - Space page: photos, prices (display only), amenities, hours, contact, announcements, live
    status — available, full
    or closed now, never a seat count (verified spaces) — and "last updated" per fact.
    - Verified / unverified spaces: every space is listed whether or not its owner has joined.

    > ## Not in v1

    > Do not build these, even partially. The data model leaves room for some of them (see [ADR
    0002](../architecture/decisions/0002-authorization-model.md) and
    [data-model.md](../architecture/data-model.md)), but
    no code for them exists in v1.

    - Online payment. Printed invoices or receipts.
